        "original_id": "2aa36126-892d-5c10-b9e6-e87ab7aa5c90",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Fancy Free, Elvira, Ain't Living Long Like This\n- People: Dallas Frazier\n- Organizations: The Oak Ridge Boys\n- Topics: album releases, singles, chart performance\n\nFacts:\n- Fancy Free is the fifth country studio album by The Oak Ridge Boys, and it was released on March 26, 1981.\n- In 1981, The Oak Ridge Boys made \"Elvira\" a famous country and pop hit, and the song is considered one of their signature songs.\n- Dallas Frazier wrote the song \"Elvira.\"\n- The songs \"Elvira,\" \"Baby Better Start Turnin' 'Em Down,\" and \"(Now and Then, There's) A Fool Such as I\" were released as singles.\n- \"Elvira,\" \"Baby Better Start Turnin' 'Em Down,\" and \"(Now and Then, There's) A Fool Such as I\" all failed to chart within the top 40.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
